<title>JAPAN: Japan Dec large store sales down 2.1 pct yr/yr. [CORRECTED 05:32 GMT]</title>
<headline>Japan Dec large store sales down 2.1 pct yr/yr. [CORRECTED 05:32 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sales at Japanese department stores and supermarkets fell 2.1 percent (corrects from 0.3 percent) in December from a year earlier to 2.74 trillion yen, the Ministry of International Trade and Industry said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The ministry also said retail sales in the whole of 1996 declined 0.4 percent from the previous year to 22.98 trillion yen, marking the fifth consecutive year of decline.  </p>
<p>A breakdown of year-on-year changes:</p>
<p>			     DEC	     NOV (REVISED)</p>
<p>  Department stores    -1.0	     +1.4</p>
<p>  Supermarkets	   -3.2	     -2.0</p>
<p>  Total		    -2.1	     -0.3</p>
</text>
